# This overlay is consumed by the ChromiumOS/Portage build system and the
# kernel patches are fed to `git apply`. Both require LF endings.
#
# The repo is commonly checked out on Windows where a global
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites LF -> CRLF in the working tree. That silently
# breaks things: `git apply` rejects CRLF patches with a misleading context
# mismatch, a shell script with a CRLF shebang fails with "bad interpreter",
# and a sourced make.conf picks up a trailing \r in variable values.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
